WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.250 --> 00:00:05.760
Camilo and Pablo Dunoyer came to America as
small children with their parents.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:09.800
My only memories are in this country, there's
nothing out there in Columbia for me.

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:14.100
I do feel like I'm American, I've assimilated
into this country completely.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.560
I mean I've lived here all my life.

00:00:16.560 --> 00:00:19.720
In the late 90s their father Roberto was a
government employee

00:00:19.720 --> 00:00:22.180
working for Columbia's Finance Minister.

00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:25.910
And a local guerilla tied to the FARC was
extorting him.

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.080
They wanted him to funnel money to them from
the treasury.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:34.740
The FARC finances it's operations through
kidnapping, ransom, extortion and drug trafficking.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.780
When he refused to help steal money from the
government, the group threatened his family.

00:01:00.640 --> 00:01:02.620
The local police said they couldn’t protect
them,

00:01:02.620 --> 00:01:06.080
so the Dunoyers fled to America on a travel visa.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:08.340
The family has been here ever since.

00:01:08.340 --> 00:01:09.340
They own a house.

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:14.100
Roberto and his wife Consuela both work at
American companies and pay their taxes.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.320
Their oldest son Pablo is a college student
majoring in engineering,

00:01:17.320 --> 00:01:20.960
and Camilo is a senior in high school where
he was elected prom king.

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:23.160
Neither have memory of their birth country.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.700
But changes in federal immigration policy
mean that this family

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.939
will likely be forced to leave America

00:01:28.940 --> 00:01:30.380
before the end of the year.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.650
If I were to be sent back there I wouldn't
be able to communicate

00:01:33.650 --> 00:01:37.920
I wouldn't be able to live normally, everything,
every opportunity will be taken away

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:40.800
it's not the same there, it's a third world
country over there.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.320
And the possibility of even being murdered
over there is a high chance.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.920
When they arrived, the Dunoyers applied for
asylum.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.619
After a multi-year legal battle, they were
denied

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:55.560
on the ground that Dunoyer’s political
views weren’t the primary factor

00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:57.560
in his decision to flee Colombia.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:01:59.340
And then through a personal connection

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:04.020
the Dunoyers were introduced to San Diego
Congressman Duncan L. Hunter.

00:02:04.020 --> 00:02:08.800
He was moved by their story and agreed to
use a special privilege, called a “private bill,”

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.200
that allows a Congress member to request deferred
deportation in specific cases.

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:19.450
Congress members have filed such private bills
on behalf of more than 1,900 immigrants since 1983.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:23.780
Hunter used the power 13 times in his 28-year
Congressional career.

00:02:23.780 --> 00:02:28.580
After he retired, the congressman’s son,
Duncan D. Hunter, was elected to the same seat

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:33.080
and he has continued filing paperwork every
year to keep the family in the U.S.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:37.740
Hunter, like his father, is a conservative
republican and hardline restrictionist.

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.700
Seal off the border first, you have to build
a wall, you gotta do E-Verify

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:42.760
so we know we're only hiring American citizens.

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.340
He’s on the record opposing birthright citizenship

00:02:45.340 --> 00:02:50.680
and co-sponsored a bill that would reduce
the number of refugees and unskilled immigrants

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:52.440
allowed in the United States.

00:02:52.440 --> 00:02:54.700
I would not increase the number of refugees
right now at all

00:02:54.700 --> 00:02:58.760
or, period, the number of immigrants coming
into the country legally right now.

00:02:58.769 --> 00:03:01.750
Sorry that people come from bad places and
not every place is America.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:02.780
That's not my fault.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.860
But Hunter believes that members of congress

00:03:04.860 --> 00:03:10.240
should have the discretionary power to grant
certain families, like the Dunoyers, political asylum.

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:14.940
It's a power that Donald Trump reined in with
an executive order signed last January

00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:17.860
that limited ICE’s discretion to defer deportations,

00:03:17.860 --> 00:03:21.720
even in special asylum cases championed by
members of congress.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:26.240
ICE has to show discretion in cases like these
and discernment.

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:30.120
But discernment is exactly what the Trump
administration hoped eliminate

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:35.680
with its executive order and Homeland security
memo announcing new zero tolerance policies.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:42.880
I have put in place a zero tolerance policy
for illegal entry on our southwest border.

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:48.240
How do you explain an apparent contradiction
in using your powers as a congressman

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:51.040
to shepherd this particular family through

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:57.040
but on the other hand supported policies that
do make it more difficult for asylum seekers.

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.180
I don't see any problem with that whatsoever,
there's no contradiction

00:04:00.180 --> 00:04:03.520
I'm elected to use my judgement on these things

00:04:03.520 --> 00:04:07.120
and I think it's the same as, we help lots
of veterans

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:10.390
a lot of guys fall through the cracks and
I'm the only one that can help them

00:04:10.390 --> 00:04:12.780
and I use my judgement and the staff uses
their judgement here

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:18.120
to determine which of those cases merit the
time and effort to do that.

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:19.739
And this was one of those cases.

00:04:19.739 --> 00:04:23.710
To this day, the Dunoyer family receives threatening
letters from the FARC

00:04:23.710 --> 00:04:26.520
which are forwarded by a relative in Colombia.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:30.360
You need to know that our organization is
not played, reads one letter,

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:35.280
we will begin to crush and dismember one by
one the members of your family;

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.820
this in order for you to pay what you have
agreed with us.

00:04:38.830 --> 00:04:44.410
As a 17 year old reading that someone wants
to basically dismember your family

00:04:44.410 --> 00:04:49.460
and that their goal is to ruin your lives
and just make your life a living hell

00:04:49.460 --> 00:04:54.740
it's just, it's terrible, it's awful, there's
no way to express it.

00:04:54.740 --> 00:05:00.520
ICE is aware of this threat, they've seen
these letters and despite all this

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:01.940
they still want to send us back.

00:05:03.260 --> 00:05:07.280
And now Congressman Hunter can no longer protect
the family from deportation

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.840
thanks to Trump's zero tolerance policies.

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.620
According to the Dunoyers,

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:15.680
an ICE agent told them to prepare to leave
the country within two weeks

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:20.180
following their next check-in with the agency,
which is yet to be scheduled.

00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:25.860
What are you worried might happen if you did
have to return to Columbia now?

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:33.800
It's a hard question it is.

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:44.660
How we throw away 17 years into oblivion and
start over it's difficult.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:49.980
No, I don't know, I don't know.

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:52.380
While Hunter is sympathetic to the plight
of the family

00:05:52.389 --> 00:05:55.010
and says he wants to do what he can to help
them,

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:59.800
he remains opposed to any measures that would
make it easier for immigrants to enter the country.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:05.680
There's lots of people that are seeking asylum
that might not be politicians

00:06:05.680 --> 00:06:10.060
but they're fleeing violence, they're fleeing
cartel violence, gang violence-

00:06:10.060 --> 00:06:11.580
Everybody's fleeing something.

00:06:11.580 --> 00:06:15.960
Lots of these people arriving at the border
might be legitimate asylum seekers

00:06:15.960 --> 00:06:20.060
and they're just being either detained or
turned back, do you think that's a problem?

00:06:20.060 --> 00:06:24.320
I see what your'e saying, no I don't think
that that's a big problem.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:29.380
Once again this family got a visa to come
into the United States first.

00:06:29.380 --> 00:06:34.980
Do you think that they definition of asylum
should be expanded a little bit to take into people-

00:06:34.980 --> 00:06:38.760
No, no I think it's very simple, ICE needs to not
be stupid.

00:06:38.760 --> 00:06:44.160
Because you have the same cases when you have
translators from Iraq and Afghanistan

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:47.610
and now Syria and Kurdistan, you have these
translators that have been helping us

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:51.979
and this is really big in Iraq and Afghanistan,
many military officers go to bat

00:06:51.979 --> 00:06:54.000
to try to get their translators back over
to the US.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.880
So you would think out of anybody in the world,

00:06:56.880 --> 00:07:03.820
who would have frontline permissions to having
asylum and becoming a US citizen,

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:06.880
it's somebody that helped us for years with
the US military,

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:10.980
was seen in their towns and villages in Iraq
and Afghanistan

00:07:10.980 --> 00:07:13.300
families being killed, death threats every
day,

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:16.020
everybody knows that they're working with
the Americans.

00:07:16.020 --> 00:07:22.380
And they don't get ahead of the normal line,
there are some cases but not all the time

00:07:22.380 --> 00:07:25.900
and that's one of those dumb things too, that's
a mistake.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:30.840
Pablo and Camilo Dunoyer are hoping that somehow
the family will be allowed to stay.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:34.560
This country has, in a way, given us safety.

00:07:34.560 --> 00:07:37.920
And we're thankful for that, we really are,
we can't express that enough

00:07:37.920 --> 00:07:40.780
the people who have come out and help us,
people like Duncan Hunter,

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:42.300
it's all the people in this community.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:45.640
Unfortunately right now the people who have
the power over us

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:50.360
and who hold our lives in their hands aren't
able to see it the way everyone else is seeing it.

00:07:50.360 --> 00:07:51.660
And it's very frustrating.

